        <div class="letter-salam">Assalamu 'Alaikum wa Rahmatullāhi wa Barākatuh</div>
        <p>I am pleased to formally invite you to join COAP | Da'awatul-Rusul, a non-profit, non-governmental organization dedicated to sharing Islam and reviving the eternal truth that all prophets were sent to convey. Established by the grace of Allāh, our organization operates upon the prophetic methodology of knowledge, sincerity, patience, wisdom, and mercy.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">We believe that every prophet—from Adam to Noah, Abraham to Moses, Jesus to Muhammad, peace be upon them all—came with one singular message: the worship of Allāh alone, the upholding of justice, and the invitation to righteousness. Our mission is to carry forward this sacred legacy in our time.</p>
        <div style="font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--primary); margin: 1.2rem 0; text-align: center;">"Who is better in speech than one who calls to Allāh, does righteousness, and says, 'Indeed, I am among the Muslims.'" (Qur'an 41:33)</div>
        <div><strong>Abou Zubairah Farooq Ibn Njalale</strong><br>Chief Executive Officer</div>
    </div>

    <!-- NEW: Complete mission statement - The truth, COAP meaning, Salaf al-Ṣāliḥah -->
    <div class="truth-mission-block" data-aos="fade-up">
        <h3>COAP | Da'awatul-Rusul <span style="font-size: 1.4rem;">— Calling of All Prophets, Call of the Messengers</span></h3>
        <div class="subhead">Reviving and Sharing The Truth according to the understanding of the righteous predecessors (Salaf al-Ṣāliḥah)</div>
        <p>COAP | Da'awatul-Rusul is a non-profit, community‑based initiative whose name carries a prophetic message. <strong class="highlight">COAP stands for Calling of All Prophets</strong>, and <strong class="highlight">Da'awatul‑Rusul</strong> is Arabic for <em>Call of the Messengers</em>. Together, the name expresses one universal invitation: to return to the original truth that every prophet — from Adam to Noah, Abraham to Moses, Jesus to Muhammad (peace be upon them all) — brought to humanity. The organization’s core mission is simple yet profound: <strong>Reviving and Sharing The Truth</strong> — not as newly invented ideas, but as understood and lived by the first three generations (Salaf al-Ṣāliḥah).</p>
        
        <p style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">The truth that all prophets called upon is not a new message. It is the oldest and most essential call in human history: to know, love, and worship Allāh alone, and to live a life of justice, mercy, and sincerity. Reviving this truth means restoring the pure, original teachings of Islam exactly as Allāh revealed them and exactly as His prophets delivered them — without changes, additions, or distortions.</p>
        
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">In practical terms, this includes three main elements. First, <strong>Tawḥīd</strong> — the belief that Allāh is One and only He deserves to be worshipped, without any partners, idols, or false gods. Second, <strong>following the Qur'an and authentic Sunnah</strong> — the Qur'an as Allāh's final book, and the Sunnah as the way of Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). Third, <strong>removing falsehood, misconceptions, and innovations</strong> — gently clearing away incorrect ideas and religious practices that distance people from true Islam.</p>
        
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">A key part of reviving the truth is following the understanding of the <strong>first three generations (Salaf al-Ṣāliḥah)</strong>. These are the Companions of the Prophet (Ṣaḥābah), their immediate successors (Tābi‘ūn), and the successors of those successors (Tābi‘ al-Tābi‘īn). The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) praised them, saying: <em>"The best of my community are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."</em> COAP | Da'awatul-Rusul therefore adopts the interpretation of the Qur'an and Sunnah as understood by these righteous predecessors, avoiding later innovations and divisions.</p>
        
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">To achieve its goal, the organization focuses on five key actions: calling people to worship Allāh alone, explaining right from wrong with knowledge and wisdom, upholding justice and good character, defending the truth with patience and gentle guidance, and firmly adhering to the way of the Salaf al-Ṣāliḥah. The method is not about arguing, insulting, or dividing people. Instead, it is built on guidance (showing the way without force), mercy (kindness even when others are harsh), and reform (improving hearts and communities, not just winning debates). All of this is done only to seek the pleasure of Allāh, not fame, money, or power.</p>
        
        <p style="margin-top: 1.2rem; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-top: 1rem;">COAP | Da'awatul-Rusul stands as a reminder that the message of all prophets is one and the same: worship Allāh alone, live justly and mercifully, and follow the Qur'an and Sunnah as understood by the first three generations (Salaf al-Ṣāliḥah). By reviving and sharing this truth with wisdom, patience, and sincerity, the organization invites every person to return to the pure, unaltered path of their Lord. In a world filled with confusion and division, COAP | Da'awatul-Rusul offers a clear, gentle, and merciful call — the call of all prophets, preserved by the righteous predecessors, for all people, until the end of time.</p>
    </div>

